# STRESS 05 — SIZING
#
# fill, fill(n), percentages, auto, fixed, min-height, max-height, and five
# levels of nesting.
#
# The claim being tested is DESIGN.md D2: every split of space goes through
# geom.DistributeTicks, which guarantees the parts sum to the whole EXACTLY.
# So the right edge of the last column in each row below must be the right
# edge of the row, with no crack and no overhang, at every page size. Rebuild
# with --page-size a4 or --page-size '200mm 300mm' and check again — those are
# widths that divide badly.

page
  size: letter
  margin: 0.45in

defaults
  font: IBM Plex Mono
  font-size: 7pt
  color: gray(0.12)

style bar
  height: 26pt
  border-width: 0.4pt
  border-color: gray(0.55)
  valign: middle
  align: center

section
  height: 28pt
  text "05 · SIZING"
    font-size: 14pt
    font-weight: bold
    tracking: 1.2pt

section
  height: 20pt
  text "fill weights. Six columns whose weights are 1, 2, 3, 1, 0.5 and 0.25 — a total of 7.75 shares of the content width."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 34pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
      text "fill"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill(2)
    box
      style: bar
      text "fill(2)"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill(3)
    box
      style: bar
      text "fill(3)"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill(1)
    box
      style: bar
      text "fill(1)"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill(0.5)
    box
      style: bar
      text "0.5"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill(0.25)
    box
      style: bar
      text ".25"
        align: center

section
  height: 22pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Percentages. 10 + 15 + 25 + 50 = 100, and the sum is exact rather than nearly exact."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 34pt
  column
    width: 10%
    box
      style: bar
      text "10%"
        align: center
  column
    width: 15%
    box
      style: bar
      text "15%"
        align: center
  column
    width: 25%
    box
      style: bar
      text "25%"
        align: center
  column
    width: 50%
    box
      style: bar
      text "50%"
        align: center

section
  height: 22pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Mixed: two fixed columns, one percentage, and two fills sharing what is left. Fixed and percentage are taken out first."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 34pt
  column
    width: 72pt
    box
      style: bar
      text "72pt"
        align: center
  column
    width: 1in
    box
      style: bar
      text "1in"
        align: center
  column
    width: 20%
    box
      style: bar
      text "20%"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
      text "fill"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill(2)
    box
      style: bar
      text "fill(2)"
        align: center

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Extremes. 1% of 522pt is 5.22pt and survives; the remaining 99% is one column. A total above 100% overflows and is an error, so it is not on this sheet."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 30pt
  column
    width: 1%
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: 99%
    box
      style: bar
      text "99%"
        align: center

section
  height: 40pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Heights on a 158pt band. Left: fixed, percentage, auto, and two fills sharing the remainder. Right: min-height and max-height, which clamp an auto or a fill child and are IGNORED on a fixed height — a fixed length freezes the child before the bounds pass runs."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 158pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 40pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "40pt"
        align: center
    box
      height: 20%
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "20%"
        align: center
    box
      height: auto
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      align: center
      text "auto"
        align: center
    box
      height: fill
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "fill"
        align: center
    box
      height: fill(2)
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "fill(2)"
        align: center

  # min-height and max-height clamp whatever the other rules produced.
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: auto
      min-height: 54pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      align: center
      text "auto, min-height 54pt"
        align: center
    box
      height: 60pt
      max-height: 30pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "60pt + max-height 30pt: still 60pt"
        align: center
    box
      height: fill
      max-height: 30pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "fill, max-height 30pt"
        align: center
    box
      height: fill
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      align: center
      text "fill takes the rest"
        align: center

section
  height: fill
  valign: bottom
  text "min-height and max-height are honoured on `auto` and `fill` children and IGNORED on a fixed height: ResolveAxis freezes a fixed child in step 2, before the bounds pass in step 6 ever looks at it. Sheet 05b carries nesting, gap and the box model."
    font-size: 6.5pt
    color: gray(0.5)
